        "text": "39"
      },
      {
        "y": 24.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 481.5,
        "tag": "title",
        "text": "History: since the dawn of civilisation"
      },
      {
        "y": 70.7,
        "x0": 75.1,
        "x1": 297.8,
        "tag": "title",
        "text": "A History – the great and the ordinary"
      },
      {
        "y": 129,
        "x0": 108.2,
        "x1": 390.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Archaeologists1 patiently work among the remains of past civilisations,"
      },
      {
        "y": 140.5,
        "x0": 108.3,
        "x1": 371.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "trying to understand once-powerful vast empires2, kingdoms3 and"
      },
      {
        "y": 152,
        "x0": 108.2,
        "x1": 386.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "dynasties4. Since the dawn5 of civilisation, societies have recorded the"
      },
      {
        "y": 163.5,
        "x0": 108.2,
        "x1": 401.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "reigns6 of kings and emperors, the fate of their heirs7 and successors8 and"
      },
      {
        "y": 175,
        "x0": 108.2,
        "x1": 395.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "major events such as coronations9, wars and conquests10. All this can be"
      },
      {
        "y": 186.5,
        "x0": 108.2,
        "x1": 408.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "recorded in manuscripts11 or on stone tablets. When an heir succeeds to the"
      },
      {
        "y": 199.1,
        "x0": 108.2,
        "x1": 407.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "throne and is crowned, we usually learn how long he/she reigns. Meanwhile,"
      },
      {
        "y": 209.5,
        "x0": 108.2,
        "x1": 408.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "the lives of the ordinary people, the peasants12 and labourers13, the pattern"
      },
      {
        "y": 221,
        "x0": 108.2,
        "x1": 396,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "of their days, the migrations14 of social groups, often go unrecorded, and"
      },
      {
        "y": 233.6,
        "x0": 108.2,
        "x1": 400.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "archaeologists and historians have a tougher task in interpreting whatever"
      },
      {
        "y": 244,
        "x0": 108.2,
        "x1": 380.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "shreds15 of evidence remain. But for many, this is the real history and"
      },
      {
        "y": 256.6,
        "x0": 108.2,
        "x1": 255,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "archaeology, the true key to our past."
      },
      {
        "y": 280.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 503.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "1 person who studies the material evidence of past societies 2 group of countries ruled by a single person"
      },
      {
        "y": 292.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 517.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "3 individual countries ruled by a king or queen 4 different rulers who are all from the same family, or a period"
      },
      {
        "y": 304.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 497.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "of time that a country is controlled by them 5 beginning 6 period that a king, queen or emperor rules"
      },
      {
        "y": 316.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 513.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "7 person who is legally entitled to continue the work of someone important who has died or who has the same"
      },
      {
        "y": 328.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 514.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "position as they had 8 person who takes over from another person 9 event when a king or queen receives"
      },
      {
        "y": 340.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 503.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "his/her crown 10 when someone or an army defeats and takes over another country 11 texts written by"
      },
      {
        "y": 352.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 508.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "hand 12 person who works on the land and earns little, usually having a low social status 13 person who"
      },
      {
        "y": 364.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 516.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "does unskilled manual work 14 moving from one place to another in large numbers 15 very small amounts"
      },
      {
        "y": 383.6,
        "x0": 74.7,
        "x1": 178.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "B Historical eras"
      },
      {
        "y": 401.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 512.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "In ancient Egypt, the Bronze Age began about 5,000 years ago. [period when the metals copper and tin"
      },
      {
        "y": 414.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 438.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "began to be used to make weapons, tools, etc.; we also talk of the Stone Age, the Iron Age]"
      },
      {
        "y": 425.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 450.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Life in medieval times was hard. [of or from the European Middle Ages, i.e. 1000–1500 AD]"
      },
      {
        "y": 437.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 517.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "I love the great Renaissance art of Italy. [period of new growth of interest and activity in the arts especially"
      },
      {
        "y": 450.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 245.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "in Europe in the 14th to 16th centuries]"
      },
      {
        "y": 461.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 506.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Magnificent architecture and works of art were created in Central America in the pre-colonial era."
      },
      {
        "y": 473.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 441.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "[period before Europeans arrived in large numbers and took power; opp. = post-colonial]"
      },
      {
        "y": 492.1,
        "x0": 75,
        "x1": 184.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "C Military history"
      },
      {
        "y": 509.8,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 266.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "infantry: soldiers on foot (uncountable)"
      },
      {
        "y": 521.8,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 289,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "cavalry: soldiers on horseback (uncountable)"
      },
      {
        "y": 533.8,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 350.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "(suit of) armour: metal protective clothing worn by soldiers"
      },
      {
        "y": 545.8,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 484.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "chariot: two-wheeled vehicle pulled by a horse and used in ancient times for racing and war"
      },
      {
        "y": 557.8,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 454.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "galleon: large sailing ship with three or four masts, used in the 15th to 18th centuries"
      },
      {
        "y": 577.6,
        "x0": 74.4,
        "x1": 137.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "D People"
      },
      {
        "y": 595.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 473.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "warlord: a military leader who controls a country or, more often, an area within a country"
      },
      {
        "y": 607.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 487.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "slave: person legally owned by someone else and who has to work for them (noun = slavery)"
      },
      {
        "y": 619.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 204.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "ruler: leader of a country"
      },
      {
        "y": 631.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 516.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "explorer: someone who travels to places that no one is thought ever to have visited, in order to find"
      },
      {
        "y": 643.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 170,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "out what is there"
      },
      {
        "y": 655.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 504.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "merchant: someone who buys and sells things in large amounts, especially by trading with other"
      },
      {
        "y": 667.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 138.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "countries"
      },
      {
        "y": 679.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 505.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "monarch: neutral term for a king or queen (a country with a king or queen at its head can also be"
      },
      {
        "y": 691.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 181.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "called a monarchy)"
      },
      {
        "y": 703.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 418.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "the nobility: collective term for people of the highest social rank in a society"
      }
    ],
